KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ reference: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ const reference: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [over.match.class.deduct]/1.1, [temp.deduct.call]/3: the deduction
guide formed from the constructor S(W<T> &) deduces T = int from the lvalue
w of type W<int>.  The front end finds no deduction for a constructor
parameter that is a reference to a template-id ("found no match for symbol
'S', candidates are: ..."); by value, `T &' and `T *' work.  libstdc++ 13's
__do_vformat_to declares `_Formatting_scanner __scanner(__ctx, __fmt);'
with the constructor _Formatting_scanner(basic_format_context<_Out, _CharT>
&, basic_string_view<_CharT>), so its body is dropped (seen with
--verbosity 9 in the <format> reductions, after
cpp_function_template_default_argument_on_earlier_declaration).
Pre-existing (bin53).  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it
fails only its WRONG assertion.
